{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>\"Take a calf of the herd for yourself\"</b> — Moses our teacher was commanded concerning these offerings, as it says at the end, \"This is the thing that HaShem commanded you to do.\" And if this was not mentioned explicitly, so too \"Moses said, 'This is the thing that HaShem commanded: Fill an omer of it for your generations' keeping\" (Exodus 16:32), and likewise \"I am the El of Beth-El\" (Genesis 31:13) — Jacob recounted this, yet the original statement to him was not mentioned. And I have already shown you in the sections on the commandment of Paschal offering (Exodus 11:1) many cases like these."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Ramban illustrates a recurring biblical phenomenon: a command or statement is referenced as having been given, yet the biblical text does not record the original communication. His cross-reference to Exodus 11:1 likely points to his commentary there discussing similar cases of unrecorded prior divine speech."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:56.465369810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}